// tests-types-04: an overflowing float literal parses to inf, which the
// printer writes as text the parser refuses, so `graphix fmt` calls a valid
// program a formatter bug.
//
// The literal parser (graphix-types/src/expr/parser/mod.rs:662, and
// literal_pattern, patternexp.rs:257) takes netidx's parse_value, whose flt
// (../netidx/netidx-value/src/parser.rs:388) turns `1e400` into inf with
// str::parse. Literal (graphix-types/src/expr/print.rs:353) prints only a
// finite f64 bare; inf goes through fmt_ext as `f64:inf`, which flt does not
// accept. An out-of-range integer (`u8:300`, `99999999999999999999`) is
// refused at parse instead. The round-trip proptest never draws a non-finite
// float: proptest 1.11's any::<f64>() covers only the finite classes.
//
// command: graphix fmt --stdout design/review-2026-10-05/repro/tests-types-04.gx
//          (graphix --no-cache on this file prints "inf inf" and exits 0)
// expected: the parse refuses `1e400` as it refuses `u8:300`, or fmt prints
//           the file back unchanged
// observed (HEAD c722befe, debug build): exit 1,
//   design/review-2026-10-05/repro/tests-types-04.gx: formatter bug: the
//   formatted text does not parse: parse error at line: 24, column: 13 ...
//       let x = f64:inf;
//   Error: 1 file(s) could not be formatted
// The same for `-1e400`, `f64:1e309` and `f32:1e40` alone.
let x = 1e400;
let y = f32:1e40;
println("[x] [y]");
sys::exit(sys::time::after_idle(duration:100.ms, 0))
